# Overview

A quick shedding game: match the top card by [[suit]] or [[rank]] and be the first to empty your hand. Eights are wild.

# Components

![[deck-52#components]]

# Setup

- Deal {2p: 7 | *: 5} cards to each player from the [[deck]].
- Turn the next card face up to start the [[discard pile]]; the rest is the [[stock]].

# Play

! On your turn, play a card matching the top discard by suit or rank, or play an 8 and name any suit.

- If you can't play, draw from the [[stock]] until you can.
- {2p} If the [[stock]] runs out, play passes when you can't play.

# End of the game

! The first player to empty their hand wins the round.

## Scoring {+points}

The winner scores the cards left in the other players' hands: 50 for each 8, 10 for each [[face card]], 1 for each ace, and the rank of the others. The first player to reach 100 points wins.

# Glossary

![[deck-52#glossary]]

Discard pile
: Face-up pile you play onto.

Stock
: Face-down draw pile.
